{"name":"Seascape","hex":"#77a2ad","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seascape","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A view of the sea.","A piece of art that depicts the sea or shoreline."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seascape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seascape","blocks":[{"text":"A seascape is a photograph, painting, or other work of art which depicts the sea, in other words an example of marine art. The word originated as a formation from landscape, which was first used for images of land in art. By a similar development, \"seascape\" has also come to mean actual perceptions of the sea itself. It is applied in planning contexts to geographical locations possessing a good view of the sea. Seascape aesthetics receive legal protection in terms of biodiversity/ health of the seas (the OSPAR Convention, and in terms of the visual bio-cultural seascape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/The_Wave_-_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/330px-The_Wave_-_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seascape","wikidata":"Q7441810"},{"title":"Seascape (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Seascape is a two-act play by American playwright Edward Albee. He completed it in 1974, having first developed it in 1967 as a short play named Life, the first half of a projected double bill with another play called Death. Seascape won the 1975 Pulitzer Prize for Drama."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seascape_(play)","wikidata":"Q7441811"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Winslow_Homer_Summer_Squall.jpg/500px-Winslow_Homer_Summer_Squall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Winslow_Homer_Summer_Squall.jpg/1280px-Winslow_Homer_Summer_Squall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Winslow_Homer_Summer_Squall.jpg/500px-Winslow_Homer_Summer_Squall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Summer Squall, 1904. A seascape by Winslow Homer.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWinslow_Homer_Summer_Squall.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Clifton_Beach_5.jpg/500px-Clifton_Beach_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Clifton_Beach_5.jpg/1280px-Clifton_Beach_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Clifton_Beach_5.jpg/500px-Clifton_Beach_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A seascape photograph at Clifton Beach, South Arm, Tasmania, Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClifton_Beach_5.jpg"}],"sounds":{"seascape":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-seascape.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-seascape.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-seascape.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-seascape.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-seascape.wav.ogg"}]}}}